---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Privacy" dek="Nothing to sign up for, nothing to type in, no adverts and no counter. What a browser fetches from other sites, and how the people in the family are shown.">
  <div class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lead">This site never asks you anything. There is no account, no form and no
      search box that sends a word anywhere, and there are no adverts. Nobody is counting who reads it.</p>
      <p class="dim">Last checked 4 November 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="wrap pv">
      <h2>What your browser fetches from elsewhere</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Fonts</b>, from Google Fonts. Google can see your IP address and which fonts were asked for.</li>
        <li><b>GitHub Pages</b> serves the site and keeps its usual server logs.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Everything else, the pictures, the maps and the charts, is part of the site itself. Following a
      link to one of the grown-up archives, or to FamilySearch or a newspaper, takes you to that site, under
      its own terms and not these.</p>

      <h2>The people in it</h2>
      <p>Anyone still living is shown by initials only, with no dates and no birth year. The family roles
      (Mum, Dad, Grandma, Grandpa) and the towns are kept, because they carry the story and neither picks out a
      person alone. People who have died are named in full. No photograph of a living person appears anywhere.</p>
      <p>If something here is wrong, or someone would rather not be named, tell us and it will be fixed.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .pv h2 { margin: 2rem 0 .6rem; }
  .pv p, .pv ul { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .pv li { margin-bottom: .5rem; }
</style>
